  1033	    # them first was a design bug: on 2026-10-20 a slow `op read` under launchd held the
  1034	    # startup path for minutes, so the port never opened and the service looked dead
  1035	    # while the process was perfectly healthy. Binding first means /stats answers at
  1036	    # once, a span that cannot be forwarded is counted rather than lost, and the thing
  1037	    # is diagnosable from outside. KeyCache's backoff keeps the retries cheap.
